/T (A child who may hesitate to speak in a group can behave quite differently when speaking to one person. Volunteers learn as much about patience, explanation and communication as the students do. The programme also remains affected by connectivity, access to devices, participation and dropouts. The next challenge is to improve the programme without losing the simple part that makes it work: one child and one volunteer having enough space to read, talk and learn together.)
/E (A child who may hesitate to speak in a group can behave quite differently when speaking to one person. Volunteers learn as much about patience, explanation and communication as the students do. The programme also remains affected by connectivity, access to devices, participation and dropouts. The next challenge is to improve the programme without losing the simple part that makes it work: one child and one volunteer having enough space to read, talk and learn together.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [8]
