/T (Early prototypes focused on structured worksheets with clear bounding boxes for student responses, i.e. input standardization. Initially, complex rule-based image processing techniques were developed and used, working reasonably well for dark pen inputs and clear/well-taken pictures of worksheets, but failing for low contrast, camera distortions / blurring and variable lighting - all of which are to be reasonably expected - giving us an average processing accuracy of 65-75% in real-world settings.)
/E (Early prototypes focused on structured worksheets with clear bounding boxes for student responses, i.e. input standardization. Initially, complex rule-based image processing techniques were developed and used, working reasonably well for dark pen inputs and clear/well-taken pictures of worksheets, but failing for low contrast, camera distortions / blurring and variable lighting - all of which are to be reasonably expected - giving us an average processing accuracy of 65-75% in real-world settings.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [16]
>>
